==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|peri|-anth}}, thus "around the flower.", from {{etyl|fr}} {{term|lang=fr|périanthe}}, from {{etyl|NL.}} {{term|lang=la|perianthium}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{botany}} The [[sterile]] parts of a [[flower]]; collectively, the [[sepal]]s and [[petal]]s (or [[tepal]]s).
# {{context|botany|bryology}} The sterile, tubelike [[tissue]] that surrounds the female reproductive structure in a leafy [[liverwort]].
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae V|5}}
#*: Archegonia are surrounded early in their development by the juvenile '''perianth''', through the slender beak of which the elongated neck of the fertilized archegonium protrudes.

====Synonyms====
* [[perigone]]

